// The speaker amp on the way back from a sleep: passwordless restart for the
// session user.
//
// WHAT THIS ANSWERS. /etc/systemd/system/razer-speakers.service programs the
// ALC298 vendor registers that switch the internal speakers on, and a
// suspend/resume resets the codec, so
// hypr/custom/scripts/after-resume.sh RESTARTS that system unit on every wake.
// Restarting a system unit from a session is a polkit request
// (org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units, verb=restart) which for a plain
// session user answers auth_admin, so every wake put the shell's polkit agent
// on screen asking for the admin password -- and because that dialog sits on
// top of the lock screen it also swallowed the password typed to unlock.
// Measured 2026-10-13, and the caller named by polkitd itself:
//
//     FAILED to authenticate to gain authorization for action
//     org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units for system-bus-name::1.15172
//     [systemctl restart razer-speakers.service] (owned by unix-user:matrix)
//
// WHY A RULE AND NOT A DIFFERENT CALL. The register writes need root: the
// codec's hwdep node /dev/snd/hwC1D0 is root:audio with an ACL that refuses
// the session user even though they are in the audio group (measured: O_RDWR
// -> EACCES). The unit is the single writer of those registers, and its
// ExecStart/ExecStartPost already wait for the codec device -- so the resume
// path keeps calling it instead of duplicating that script's argv in the
// session, which is the duplication the resume path was written to avoid.
//
// THE SCOPE. One action, one unit name, the local active session, and the
// same narrowing the other rules here use: allow_inactive stays false, so a
// remote or background caller still authenticates. The verbs systemctl offers
// for this unit -- start, stop, restart -- are the whole grant; there is no
// path from here to another unit or to an arbitrary command.
//
// AND IT IS NOT THE ONLY DEFENCE. after-resume.sh asks with
// `systemctl --no-ask-password`, so a machine that never got this file
// installed logs a refusal instead of raising a prompt on the wake screen.
polkit.addRule(function (action, subject) {
    if (action.id !== "org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units") {
        return undefined;
    }
    if (!(subject.local && subject.active)) {
        return undefined;
    }
    if (!subject.isInGroup("wheel")) {
        return undefined;
    }
    if (action.lookup("unit") === "razer-speakers.service") {
        return "yes";
    }
    return undefined;
});
